{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"Under an approved manager-of-managers arrangement, the principal adviser may hire or replace a sub-adviser without a shareholder vote if the fund’s exemptive order and governing documents permit it, and required board approval and conditions are met. Typically, the independent trustees—and the full board—must approve the new sub-adviser and the material terms of its contract; the fund must provide required disclosure, including information about the change, in its prospectus and shareholder reports.\n\nThe principal adviser remains responsible for supervising and monitoring the sub-adviser, overseeing the fund’s overall investment program, and recommending changes when warranted. The arrangement does not delegate away the principal adviser’s fiduciary duties to the fund."}}
